steps.description:
Create packages/mull/src/adapters/relay-types.ts. Define minimal TypeScript interfaces that mirror the relay daemon's wire format for JSONL parsing. Do NOT import from the relay SDK — this keeps mull portable and avoids a runtime dependency.

Types to define:
- RelayEnvelope<T>: { id: string, type: string, timestamp: string, payload: T }
- RelaySendPayload: { from: string, to: string, body: string, thread?: string }
- RelayChannelPayload: { from: string, channel: string, body: string, thread?: string }
- RelaySpawnPayload: { name: string, cli: string, task?: string }
- RelayReleasePayload: { name: string }
- RelayMessageType: union type of 'message' | 'channel_message' | 'spawn' | 'release' | 'broadcast'

These are minimal parse targets — only the fields mull needs for extraction. Additional fields in the actual relay format are ignored by the parser.
